LineageOS for ASUS ZenFone Max Pro M2 (X01BD)
===============================================

Device Information
------------------

* **Device**: ASUS ZenFone Max Pro M2
* **Codename**: X01BD
* **Release Date**: December 2018
* **SoC**: Qualcomm Snapdragon 660 (SDM660)
* **RAM**: 3GB/4GB/6GB
* **Storage**: 32GB/64GB
* **Display**: 6.26" FHD+ (2280x1080) IPS LCD
* **Camera**: 12MP + 5MP (rear), 13MP (front)
* **Battery**: 5000mAh

Getting Started
---------------

To get started with building LineageOS for ASUS ZenFone Max Pro M2, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

### Initialize Repository

To initialize your local repository using the LineageOS trees for X01BD:
```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/AOSPInsider/android.git -b fourteen-asus --git-lfs
```

### Sync Repository
```bash
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

### Device-Specific Setup

1. **Device Tree**: `device/asus/X01BD`
2. **Vendor Blobs**: `vendor/asus/X01BD`
3. **Kernel**: `kernel/asus/X01BD`

### Building LineageOS

```bash
# Set up environment
source build/envsetup.sh

# Choose target
lunch lineage_X01BD-userdebug

# Build ROM
m bacon
```

### Notes

- This build is based on LineageOS 21.0 (Android 14)
- Make sure you have at least 200GB of free disk space
- Build time varies depending on your hardware (typically 2-6 hours)
- For troubleshooting, check the [LineageOS Wiki](https://wiki.lineageos.org/)

### Credits

Special thanks to the LineageOS team and ASUS device maintainers for their continuous work on keeping this device supported.
